      "content": "I would advise against using Tylenol to \"fast-track\" fever reduction, as this can mask symptoms rather than addressing the underlying cause. Taking more than the recommended dose can lead to liver damage or other adverse effects in excessive cases. For adults, the recommended dose of acetaminophen (Tylenol) for fever and pain is 325mg every 4-6 hours as needed. Please don't exceed this dose or take it too frequently. It's always better to consult a doctor for guidance on managing his symptoms.",
